{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/676388-protean-s-predatory-aspect-extra-sense-vs-obfuscate-s-cloak-of-night","id":676388,"title":"Protean's Predatory Aspect \"Extra Sense\" vs Obfuscate's Cloak of Night!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-24T07:58:25-07:00","id":676388,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Protean's Predatory Aspect \"Extra Sense\" vs Obfuscate's Cloak of Night!","content":"Dear ladies and gents,<br /> <br /> We were playing a <b>Vampire the Requiem: Second Edition </b>session the other day with my pals and <i>this </i>came up:<br /> <br /> - <i>Could a <b>Gangrel </b>using <b>Protean's (II) Predatory Aspect - &quot;Extra Sense&quot;</b> be able to sense another Kindred using <b>Obfuscate's (III) Cloak of Night</b> to mask himself?</i><br /> <br /> <u>Some facts from the official Rulebook:</u><br /> <br /> <b>Obfuscate - General info: </b>&quot;<b>Mixed Signals:</b> Obfuscate tricks the victim\u2019s mind directly, removing traces of the vampire from the sensory information reaching her brain, rather than fooling her senses directly. Obfuscate affects <b>smell </b>and <b>taste</b> as much as <b>sight </b>or <b>hearing</b>...&quot; (4 <i>main</i> senses mentioned here)<br /> <br /> <b>Obfuscate's (III) - Cloak of Night: </b>&quot;If another vampire manages to perceive him, through Auspex, attack,<i><b> or any other means</b></i>, she can sense his predatory aura and lash out&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Protean's (II) Predatory Aspect - &quot;Extra Sense&quot;:</b> &quot;The Kindred grows <b>extra </b>sensory organs, giving her tremor sense, echolocation, or some other sense that allows her to \u201csee\u201d without using her eyes. Using this (<b>extra</b>) <b>sense</b>, she has a 360-degree field of vision.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> The question at hand goes like this; Would a Gangrel using his &quot;Extra Sense&quot; (which has duration scene) be able to bypass the main senses that Obfuscate seemingly targets or not?<br /> <br /> <br /> Thank you in advance!<br /> <br /> With respect,<br /> Haya<br /> <br /> <br /> PS: If we could have some <i>official</i> feedback as well it would be deeply appreciated!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8056-haya-jii-san","name":"Haya-jii-san","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T08:07:48-07:00","id":676413,"title":"","content":"Something I think is relevant from the Obfuscate ability is this. 'He leaves no scent and makes no sound, though his passing leaves incidental signs, like drifting smoke or creaking floorboards.'<br /> <br /> You're still there, you're still moving. Obfuscate is trying to keep your mind from noticing. Protean gives you a supernatural sense to notice things you otherwise wouldn't. Seems like a Clash of Wills is in order. If the gangrel wins, they notice and manages to perceive the other vampire. If the other vampire wins, their Obfuscate successfully obscures them from the gangrel's extra senses.<br /> <br /> The mention of 'tremor sense' always made me think of Dungeons and Dragons, as I believe it's a monster sense there or in Pathfinder but something I don't recall ever hearing about in World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-24-2015, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T13:12:11-07:00","id":676765,"title":"","content":"In this situation i would say no, at least not with Protean 2 that gives you natural extra senses but that still that exists in nature. Obfuscate quotes 4 senses to give examples but main focus of the writing is: <b>Obfuscate tricks the victim\u2019s mind directly, removing traces of the vampire from the sensory information reaching her brain, rather than fooling her senses directly</b>. No matter what or how many sensory organs you have. Echolocation, termal vision or any other, obfuscate doesn't care becaue it tricks your mind not the organs, not how you percieve but how you interpret those perceptions.<br /> <br /> It could give a Clash of Will if you chose an extra sensory organ for your Unnatural Aspect (Protean 4), but it still doesn't click with me, because it's always a matter of perception, whereas obfuscate doesn't work on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T13:34:18-07:00","id":676835,"title":"","content":"I would allow a clash of wills for the reasons mentioned by nofather, I think you can make the case that the senses granted by Protean pick on those incidental signs that could reveal an Obfuscated vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T13:54:22-07:00","id":676849,"title":"","content":"I have no qualms allowing a Clash of Wills with Protean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T15:36:00-07:00","id":676897,"title":"","content":"While Obfuscate does work by changing the way the observer interprets information about the vampire using it, it doesn't seem to extend to information about the things the user interacts with - hence the line about leaving incidental signs of their presence. If an obfuscated vampire still causes floorboards to creak, and an observer can correctly interpret that audio information about the floorboards, then a Protean user who can sense vibrations through the ground Toff style would definitely be able to recognize that someone is there. On the other hand echolocation conveys information about the obfuscate user herself, and in my opinion would not work.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, when in doubt use Clash of Wills. That's literally what those rules exist for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T04:04:28-07:00","id":678754,"title":"","content":"Dear forum,<br /> <br /> I'd like to take the time and <i>thank you</i> for the precious feedback <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> With respect,<br /> Haya-jii","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8056-haya-jii-san","name":"Haya-jii-san","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}